<title>CANADA: Canada election opinion poll list of results.</title>
<headline>Canada election opinion poll list of results.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are results of Canada nationwide public opinion polls published since the Canadian federal election campaign began.</p>
<p>DATE POLLING	----- DECIDED VOTERS -----   UND  SMPL  MOE</p>
<p>PUBL GROUP	   LIB   PC    REF    BQ   NDP  N/A  SIZE</p>
<p> 5/27 Zogby/Reuter 40.7  22.0  18.8   6.3   9.3  29  1,115 3.0</p>
<p> 5/27 Ekos	   37.8  21.2  17.7   9.7  11.3  28  3,000 1.8</p>
<p> 5/26 Zogby/Reuter 42.2  20.6  19.3   6.3   9.9  33  1,014 3.2</p>
<p> 5/25 Zogby/Reuter 43.8  20.2  16.9   6.6  10.6  31  1,005 3.2</p>
<p> 5/16 Zogby/Reuter 45.4  20.4  15.8   7.5   9.9  29  1,009 3.2</p>
<p> 5/12 Reid/CTV/Sou 42    19    18     9    11     8  3,208 2.3</p>
<p> 5/05 Zogby/Reuter 47.6  16.2  15.4   7.7  10.2  25  1,005 3.2</p>
<p> 4/30 COMPAS/FP    47    18    13    11    10    23  2,600 1.9</p>
<p> 4/29 Environ/CROP 44    20    15     8    11    15  2,541 2.0</p>
<p>(LIB=Liberal, PC=Progressive Conservatives, REF=Reform, BQ=Bloc Quebecois, NDP=New Democratic Party, UND N/A=Undecided/No answer, MOE=Margin of Error)</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
